- component along local lateral: a positive physics pitch rotates about local +X (left axis) and takes fwd (+Z) toward −Y (down). A positive-angle rotation about +X (left): right-hand rule about +X: Y→Z, Z→−Y. So fwd → down. Therefore axis·left > 0 → nose must go down → positive pitch. left = −right. So physPitch = −axis·right (where right is the ship's right vector).

